From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kiritantakechi <kiritantakechi@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 08:03:57 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] download: depend on a package's source only being there

A package's prepared stamp depends on every file the package downloads,
so make prepares the package again whenever a download is newer than
the stamp, although its content is the one the package's hash names. A
download is newer whenever it lands after the stamp: in a fresh
download directory, or in a tree whose build directories come from a
cache, where make download runs after the stamps are restored. Every
package with restored stamps is then prepared and built again; for the
host builds of Go and Rust that is most of an hour.

The stamp's name already covers the package's own files, its Makefile
among them, which names each download and its hash: another source
always gets another stamp. So a download only has to be there when the
package is prepared. Make it an order-only prerequisite.

Covered by CI's firmware jobs, which restore the host builds of Go and
Rust before make download fetches their sources, into an empty download
directory when the download cache misses (build/ci "Toolchain cache
hit").

Signed-off-by: kiritantakechi <kiritantakechi@gmail.com>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 include/download.mk | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/include/download.mk b/include/download.mk
index 0ea08d3..75bc386 100644
--- a/include/download.mk
+++ b/include/download.mk
@@ -357,7 +357,7 @@ define Download
   )
 
   $(foreach dep,$(DOWNLOAD_RDEP),
-    $(dep): $(DL_DIR)/$(FILE)
+    $(dep): | $(DL_DIR)/$(FILE)
   )
   download: $(DL_DIR)/$(FILE)
 
